            <ArticleTitle>On call. I am 72 years old and in good health. I've had left knee pain on and off for almost six months, nothing too severe, but it aches if I walk more than a mile or so, and I sometimes get sharp pain on the stairs. My doctor sent me for an MRI of both knees; it showed &quot;mild to moderate osteoarthritis&quot; in both knees and a torn meniscus in my right knee, which feels fine. I think I know what to do about my painful knee--but what should I do for the torn meniscus in my &quot;good&quot; knee?</ArticleTitle>
